<p>This allows you to configure the settings for Perfect Binding.</p>
<p>Perfect binding is a binding method that applies heated glue to printed 
 sheets to form a book block, encloses the book block in a cover sheet, 
 and trims away excess paper to create neat edges.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about perfect binding and the supported 
 paper types and sizes, see the operating instructions provided with the 
 printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="position" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Binding Position:</span></p>
<p>Select the binding position.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="tray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Binding Paper Source Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select the paper tray from which the cover sheets will be fed.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cutopt" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Cutting Options:</span></p>
<p>Select the type of cutting (edge trimming) method to apply when finishing.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not Cut</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">No cut is applied. Edges are not trimmed.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Fore Edge (Finishing Size)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Only the fore edge is trimmed. Specify the fore 
 edge's finishing size length in the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Cut Position</span> 
 area.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Fore Edge</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Only the fore edge is trimmed. Specify the cut length 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Cut Position</span> area.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">3 Edges (Finishing Size)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">All edges except the binding edge are trimmed. Specify 
 the finishing size in the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Finishing 
 Size:</span> list. If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size</span>, 
 specify the size for <span class="Term-Soft">I. Width:</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">H. Length:</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust 
 Cut Position</span> area.</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">If you want to shift the cut position along the 
 binding edge, specify in <span class="Term-Soft">J. Along Binding Edge:</span> 
 the distance by which to shift the cut position from the center.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">3 Edges</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">All edges except the binding edge are trimmed. Specify 
 the cut lengths for <span class="Term-Soft">E. Head Edge:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">F. Tail Edge:</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">G. Fore 
 Edge:</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Cut Position</span> area. 
 </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="unit" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Measurement Unit:</span></p>
<p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">inch</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">mm</span> 
 as the measurement unit.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="adjustimage" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Position</span></p>
<p>Specify the distance by which you want to shift the print image on the 
 book block.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">C. Along Binding Edge:</span></p>
<p>Specify the distance by which to shift the print image along the binding 
 edge.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">D. Across Binding Edge:</span></p>
<p>Specify the distance by which to shift the print image across the binding 
 edge.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Cut Position</span></p>
<p>Specify settings according to the cutting (edge trimming) method selected 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Cutting Options:</span> list. 
 The shaded settings are unavailable.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="adjustcut" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">E. Head Edge:</span></p>
<p>Specify the cut length of the head edge.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">F. Tail Edge:</span></p>
<p>Specify the cut length of the tail edge.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">G. Fore Edge:</span></p>
<p>Specify the cut length of the fore edge.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">H. Page Length:</span></p>
<p>Specify the fore edge's finishing size length.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="finish" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Finishing Size:</span></p>
<p>Specify the finishing size in the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">I. Width:</span></p>
<p>Specify the size of page width for the custom paper size.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">H. Length:</span></p>
<p>Specify the size of page length for the custom paper size.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">J. Along Binding Edge:</span></p>
<p>If you want to shift the cut position along the binding edge, specify 
 the distance by which to shift the cut position from the center.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the entries and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this dialog box to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
